{#
  ============================================================================
  TEMPLATE: observation-medical-test-body_fsh.twig
  ============================================================================
  PURPOSE
    A PARTIAL TEMPLATE — a reusable body fragment included by frame templates
    using Twig's `{% include %}` directive. It must never be rendered
    standalone; it is always embedded inside another template that supplies
    the `Instance:` header and the observation category.

    Currently included by:
      observation-resultslab-eu-lab_fsh.twig   (EU lab Observation)
      observation-medical-test-result-eu_fsh.twig (MedicalTestResultEuCore)

  PARTIAL TEMPLATE STRUCTURE
    This file does NOT begin with a `%%FSH%%` marker. It starts directly with
    FSH body rules (`* id = ...`) and HTML bag calls, continuing the FSH
    instance opened by the including template. The including template provides:
      - The `%%FSH%%` section marker
      - The `Instance:` / `InstanceOf:` / `Usage:` header
      - The observation `category` coding
    This partial then provides everything from `* id` onward.

    The file ends with its own `%%HEAD%%` and `%%HTML%%` markers, which
    effectively close the section structure for the combined output.
    `%%HEAD%%` is empty; `%%HTML%%` emits the body rows.

  FIVE-COLUMN HTML TABLE
    Column 1 — Test code display        (always)
    Column 2 — Observation value        (always; number, concept display or text)
    Column 3 — Reference range          (always; "-" when none)
    Column 4 — Interpretation flag      (always; "" when not applicable)
    Column 5 — Unit                     (always; "-" when not a Quantity)

    Every branch emits exactly five cells. Before 2026-09-11 the branches
    emitted two, four or five cells against a four-column header, so rows did
    not line up. The cell values are collected into variables first and emitted
    once, at the end of the value section, so a new branch cannot get this
    wrong again.

    The column 2 header is dynamic: `addHEAD_th(labresult.report|date('d-M-Y'))`
    — the report date is used as the column header, not a static label.

  VALUE TYPE BRANCHING — Quantity, CodeableConcept, String
    The three FHIR value types are handled in ONE mutually exclusive
    if / elseif / else chain driven by `labresult.value.type`. They used to be
    two independent `if` blocks, which let a result fall into the wrong one.

    QUANTITY
        * valueQuantity.value  ← labresult.value.value   (numeric measurement)
        * valueQuantity.unit   ← labresult.value.human   (human-readable unit)
        * valueQuantity.code   ← labresult.value.unit    (UCUM code)
        * valueQuantity.system ← labresult.value.system  ("ucum", no sigil)
      `.human` falls back to `.code` when the upstream layer does not supply it.

    CODEABLE CONCEPT
        * valueCodeableConcept ← value.system # value.code "value.display"

    STRING
        * valueString ← value.value, quoted and FSH-escaped.

  SYSTEM SIGIL — TOLERANT, NOT CONVENTIONAL
    Every system value is normalised at the point of use: a bare alias gets
    exactly one `$`, an alias that already carries one is left alone, and a
    full URI or URN (anything containing ":") is passed through untouched.
    The template is therefore correct whichever convention the PHP layer uses.
    This replaces the old split where the Quantity branch prefixed `$` and the
    CodeableConcept branch did not — the mismatch that produced `$$sct` as
    soon as the upstream layer started supplying `$sct`.

  REFERENCE RANGE — EMITTED FOR EVERY VALUE TYPE
    The reference range block sits OUTSIDE the value branch. It used to live
    inside the Quantity branch only, so a coded result that needed a reference
    range was pushed into the Quantity branch and came out as a broken
    `valueQuantity`. That was the single cause of 327 of 1755 errors in run 1.

    Numeric low/high are emitted as SimpleQuantity ONLY for Quantity values,
    against `labresult.reference.system` (default "ucum"). For coded and text
    values the same bounds go into `referenceRange[+].text`, because their
    Synthea units ("{#/area}", "colony forming units per mL") are not UCUM
    codes and must not be bound to a code system.

    The interpretation flag (L / H) is derived only for numeric values.

  FSH STRING ESCAPING
    Every interpolated value that lands inside an FSH string uses
    `|replace(FSHQ)|raw`: `raw` suppresses Twig's HTML autoescape, which has no
    business in FSH and was turning "<=" into "&lt;=" inside code displays;
    `replace(FSHQ)` escapes backslashes and double quotes, which FSH does need.
    Conversely every value handed to the HTML bag uses `|e('html')`, which is
    what keeps "<=" from breaking the XHTML narrative. The two were inverted.

  EFFECTIVE DATE
    Exactly one `effectiveDateTime` is emitted: `labresult.effective` when set,
    otherwise `labresult.date`. Both used to be emitted unconditionally, and
    the second silently overwrote the first for all 1817 observations.

  BODY SITE AND SPECIMEN
    Both are conditional:
      bodySite[+] — when labresult.site is non-empty.
      specimen    — Reference to a Specimen resource by UUID when labresult.specimenid
                    is non-empty.

  CSS CLASS
    Uses `hl7__eu__lab__report` — the EU Laboratory Report stylesheet.

  CONTEXT VARIABLES  (all supplied by the including template's caller)
  ┌────────────────────────────────────┬──────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Variable                           │ Type     │ Description                                │
  ├────────────────────────────────────┼──────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ instanceid                         │ string   │ Resource id (from including template).     │
  │ labresult.report                   │ date     │ Report date; used as HTML column 2 header. │
  │ labresult.subject                  │ string   │ UUID of the subject Patient.               │
  │ labresult.subjectname              │ string   │ Subject display name.                      │
  │ labresult.code                     │ object[] │ Array of codings; only first is used.      │
  │   [0].system                       │ string   │   CodeSystem URI.                          │
  │   [0].code                         │ string   │   Observation concept code.                │
  │   [0].display                      │ string   │   Display text for column 1.               │
  │ labresult.effective                │ string?  │ Optional ISO 8601 effective date/time.     │
  │ labresult.date                     │ date     │ Report date; used as effectiveDateTime     │
  │                                    │          │ (YYYY-MM-DD) only when .effective is unset.│
  │ labresult.value                    │ object?  │ The observation value.                     │
  │   .type                            │ string   │   "Quantity", "CodeableConcept", "String". │
  │   .value                           │ number   │   Numeric measurement, or the raw text.    │
  │   .code                            │ string   │   Quantity: UCUM code. CC: SNOMED code.    │
  │   .unit                            │ string   │   UCUM unit code; "" for CC and String.    │
  │   .human                           │ string?  │   Human-readable unit; falls back to .code.│
  │   .system                          │ string   │   "ucum" / "sct" / "" — WITHOUT the $.     │
  │   .display                         │ string   │   Display when type is CodeableConcept.    │
  │ labresult.valueQuantity            │ object?  │ Alternative Quantity path (same sub-fields)│
  │ labresult.valueCodeableConcept     │ object?  │ Alternative CC path.                       │
  │   .system / .code / .display       │ string   │   CC coding fields.                        │
  │ labresult.valueString              │ string?  │ Fallback plain string value.               │
  │ labresult.reference.low            │ number?  │ Lower bound of reference range.            │
  │ labresult.reference.high           │ number?  │ Upper bound of reference range.            │
  │ labresult.reference.text           │ string?  │ Text reference range (when no low/high).   │
  │ labresult.reference.unit           │ string   │ UCUM unit code for reference range.        │
  │ labresult.reference.system         │ string?  │ Code system for the range unit, no $;      │
  │                                    │          │ defaults to "ucum".                        │
  │ labresult.site                     │ object?  │ Optional body site.                        │
  │   .system / .code / .display       │ string   │   Site coding fields.                      │
  │ labresult.specimenid               │ string?  │ Optional UUID of the Specimen resource.    │
  └────────────────────────────────────┴──────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  AUTHOR   KH
  SINCE    2025-09-02
  CHANGED  2026-09-11 — run-1 defect fixes: single value[x] branch incl. String,
           reference range lifted out of the Quantity branch, one
           effectiveDateTime, FSH/HTML escaping un-inverted, `$` sigil
           convention unified, five HTML cells in every branch.
  ============================================================================
#}

{#
  ── FSH string escaping map ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Applied as |replace(FSHQ)|raw to anything that ends up inside an FSH string.
  Backslash first, then the double quote — replace() applies the pairs in
  insertion order, and swapping them would double-escape the backslash.
#}
{% set FSHQ = {'\\': '\\\\', '"': '\\"'} %}

{#
  ── Code system sigil ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  A system arrives either as a bare alias ("loinc"), an alias that already
  carries the sigil ("$loinc"), or a full URI/URN ("urn:iso:std:iso:3166").
  Each use below normalises it to exactly one '$' for an alias and leaves a
  URI untouched, so the template is correct whichever convention the PHP
  layer uses. That removes the coupling that produced "$$sct" in run 1.
  The pattern, applied per system variable:

    {% set x = (s is empty or ':' in s or s starts with '$') ? s : '$' ~ s %}
#}

{#
  ── Resource id ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The Instance: header is provided by the including template. This partial
  begins with the id rule.
#}
* id = "{{ instanceid }}"

{#
  ── HEAD bag: four-column table header ─────────────────────────────────────
  Column 2 header is dynamic — the report date, formatted d-M-Y.
  This is the only template in the project where a HEAD column label is a
  data value rather than a static string.
#}
{{ addHEAD_tr() }}
{{ addHEAD_th("Test") }}
{{ addHEAD_th(labresult.report|date('d-M-Y')) }}
{{ addHEAD_th("Reference&#xA0;Range") }}
{{ addHEAD_th("Flag") }}
{{ addHEAD_th("Unit") }}
{{ addHEAD_trend() -}}

{{ addHTML_tr() }}

{#
  ── Fixed status ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#}
* status = #final

{#
  ── Observation code (td 1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  labresult.code is an array; |first extracts the first coding. The code
  element uses [+]/[=] indexing (code is repeatable in FHIR Observation),
  with .text set alongside the coding.
#}
{# Use first coding only — HL7 EU HDR requires exactly 1..1 code #}
{% set c = labresult.code|first %}
{% set csys = (c.system is empty or ':' in c.system or c.system starts with '$') ? c.system : '$' ~ c.system %}
* code[+].coding = {{ csys }}#{{ c.code }} "{{ c.display|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
* code[=].text = "{{ c.display|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{{ addHTML_td(c.display|e('html')) }}

{#
  ── Effective date — exactly one rule ──────────────────────────────────────
  labresult.effective carries the full timestamp and wins when present;
  labresult.date is the date-only fallback. Emitting both, as this template
  did until 2026-09-11, means the fallback silently overwrites the real
  timestamp, because SUSHI keeps the last assignment.
#}
{% if labresult.effective is not empty %}
* effectiveDateTime = "{{ labresult.effective }}"
{% else %}
* effectiveDateTime = "{{ labresult.date|date('Y-m-d') }}"
{% endif %}

{#
  ── Patient reference ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#}
* subject = Reference(urn:uuid:{{ labresult.subject }}) "{{ labresult.subjectname|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  VALUE TYPE BRANCH A — Quantity
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Triggered by type == "Quantity" or non-empty valueQuantity.
  ?? coalesces the two data paths (value.* vs valueQuantity.*).

  Variable name mapping note:
    FHIR Quantity.unit (display string) ← labresult.value.code
    FHIR Quantity.code (UCUM code)      ← labresult.value.unit
  The source variable names (.code / .unit) are swapped relative to FHIR's
  element names — this reflects the upstream data model, not an error.
#}
{#
  Resolve the value type once. The ?? chains keep the two historical data
  paths (value.* and valueQuantity.* / valueCodeableConcept.* / valueString)
  working, but the TYPE now decides the branch — a single source of truth.
#}
{% set vtype = labresult.value.type
     ?? (labresult.valueCodeableConcept is not empty ? "CodeableConcept"
        : (labresult.valueString is not empty ? "String" : "Quantity")) %}

{% set vnum  = labresult.value.value ?? labresult.valueQuantity.value %}
{% set vcode = labresult.value.code ?? labresult.valueCodeableConcept.code %}
{% set vsysraw = labresult.value.system ?? labresult.valueQuantity.system ?? labresult.valueCodeableConcept.system %}
{% set vsys = (vsysraw is empty or ':' in vsysraw or vsysraw starts with '$') ? vsysraw : '$' ~ vsysraw %}
{% set vdisp = labresult.value.display ?? labresult.valueCodeableConcept.display %}
{% set vucum = labresult.value.unit ?? labresult.valueQuantity.unit %}
{% set vhuman = labresult.value.human ?? labresult.value.code ?? labresult.valueQuantity.code %}
{% set vtext = labresult.value.value ?? labresult.valueString %}

{# HTML cells, collected here and emitted once below — always five #}
{% set tdValue = "" %}
{% set tdRange = "-" %}
{% set tdFlag  = "" %}
{% set tdUnit  = "-" %}

{% if vtype == "CodeableConcept" %}
{# ── value as CodeableConcept ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
* valueCodeableConcept = {{ vsys }}#{{ vcode }} "{{ vdisp|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{% set tdValue = vdisp|e('html') %}

{% elseif vtype == "String" %}
{# ── value as plain string — must be quoted, or the FSH parser derails ────── #}
* valueString = "{{ vtext|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{% set tdValue = vtext|e('html') %}

{% else %}
{# ── value as Quantity ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
* valueQuantity.value = {{ vnum }}
* valueQuantity.unit = "{{ vhuman|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
* valueQuantity.code = #{{ vucum }}
* valueQuantity.system = {{ vsys }}
{% set tdValue = vnum %}
{% set tdUnit = vucum|e('html') %}
{% endif %}

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  REFERENCE RANGE — for every value type
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Numeric bounds become a SimpleQuantity only for Quantity values, bound to
  labresult.reference.system (default "ucum"). For coded and text values the
  same bounds go into .text: their Synthea units are not UCUM codes and binding
  them to a code system is what produced "$$sct#{#/area}" in run 1.

  The interpretation flag is derived only where a numeric comparison is
  meaningful.
#}
{% set rsysraw = labresult.reference.system|default('ucum') %}
{% set rsys = (':' in rsysraw or rsysraw starts with '$') ? rsysraw : '$' ~ rsysraw %}

{% if labresult.reference.low is not empty and labresult.reference.high is not empty %}
{% set tdRange = (labresult.reference.low ~ " - " ~ labresult.reference.high)|e('html') %}

{% if vtype == "Quantity" %}
* referenceRange[+].low = {{ labresult.reference.low + 0 }} {{ rsys }}#{{ labresult.reference.unit }}
* referenceRange[=].high = {{ labresult.reference.high + 0 }} {{ rsys }}#{{ labresult.reference.unit }}
{% if vnum < labresult.reference.low %}
* interpretation = $v3-ObservationInterpretation#L "Low"
{% set tdFlag = "L" %}
{% elseif vnum > labresult.reference.high %}
* interpretation = $v3-ObservationInterpretation#H "High"
{% set tdFlag = "H" %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% set rtext = labresult.reference.low ~ ' - ' ~ labresult.reference.high %}
{% if labresult.reference.unit is not empty %}{% set rtext = rtext ~ ' ' ~ labresult.reference.unit %}{% endif %}
* referenceRange[+].text = "{{ rtext|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{% endif %}

{% elseif labresult.reference.text is not empty %}
{# Text-only reference range — no numeric bounds available #}
* referenceRange[+].text = "{{ labresult.reference.text|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{% set tdRange = labresult.reference.text|e('html') %}
{% endif %} {# reference range #}

{#
  ── The five HTML cells, in one place ───────────────────────────────────────
#}
{{ addHTML_td(tdValue) }}
{{ addHTML_td(tdRange) }}
{{ addHTML_td(tdFlag) }}
{{ addHTML_td(tdUnit) }}

{#
  ── Body site (conditional; FSH only) ──────────────────────────────────────
#}
{% if labresult.site is not empty %}
* bodySite[+] = {{ labresult.site.system }}#{{ labresult.site.code }} "{{ labresult.site.display|replace(FSHQ)|raw }}"
{% endif %}

{#
  ── Specimen reference (conditional) ───────────────────────────────────────
#}
{% if labresult.specimenid is not empty %}
* specimen = Reference(urn:uuid:{{ labresult.specimenid }})
{% endif %}

{{ addHTML_trend() -}}

{#
  ── FHIR narrative ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Both HEAD and HTML bags flushed — full headed table including the dynamic
  date column header. CSS class: hl7__eu__lab__report.
#}
* text.status = #generated
* text.div = """
<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<table class="hl7__eu__lab__report">{{ emitHEAD() | raw }}{{ emitHTML() | raw }}</table>
</div>
"""

%%HEAD%% {# ── Section marker — HEAD section intentionally empty for this partial ─ #}

%%HTML%% {# ── Section marker required by the FSH pre-processor ─────────────── #}
{{ emitHTML() | raw }}
